From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun55i: add A733 (sun60iw2) GMAC200 via per-SoC syscon offset

The A733 (sun60iw2) fits the same Synopsys DWC_ether_qos "GMAC200" core the
dwmac-sun55i glue already drives on the A523/T527, and its Allwinner "EMAC
clock" syscon register has the identical field layout (ETXDC/ERXDC delays,
EPIT, ETCS, RMII_EN). Only one thing differs: where that register lives.

On the A523/T527 the register sits in the shared system-control block at
offset 0x34 (the historical EMAC1 slot, same as dwmac-sun8i). On the A733 the
equivalent register is GMAC_CFG, the first register of the GMAC's own glue
block (0x04508000 + 0x00) -- system-control has no ethernet syscon on this SoC.
This was confirmed from the A733 User Manual (GMAC register list: GMAC_CFG at
glue-base offset 0x0000) and a live silicon read (0x04508000 = 0x00011146 =
external-PHY RGMII config), not from any vendor DT or driver.

The driver hard-coded the 0x34 offset. Turn it into per-compatible match data
(a small sun55i_gmac_variant) so the A733 can reuse the entire glue with its
own 0x00 offset. The existing A523 compatible keeps 0x34, so its behaviour is
unchanged. No field masks change: the A733 GMAC_CFG low bits are bit-identical
to the A523 syscon register.

(A733 GMAC_CFG also has a 2-bit ETXDC high field at [17:16] that the A523
register lacks, extending TX delay from 3 to 5 bits. This patch does not use
it -- the existing 3-bit tx-internal-delay-ps range (0..700ps) is enough to
bring the link up; wider TX delay, if a board needs it, is a separate change.)

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun55i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun55i.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/phy.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/stmmac.h>
@@ -23,7 +24,27 @@
 #include "stmmac.h"
 #include "stmmac_platform.h"
 
-#define SYSCON_REG		0x34
+/*
+ * The syscon "EMAC clock" register carries the same field layout on every
+ * sun55i-family GMAC200 (delays, EPIT, ETCS, RMII_EN below), but its offset
+ * inside the phandle-referenced regmap differs per SoC:
+ *  - A523/T527: the register lives in the shared system-control block at
+ *    offset 0x34 (the EMAC1 slot), same idiom as dwmac-sun8i.
+ *  - A733 (sun60iw2): the equivalent register is GMAC_CFG, the first register
+ *    of the GMAC's own glue block (base + 0x00), not in system-control.
+ * The offset therefore comes from per-compatible match data.
+ */
+struct sun55i_gmac_variant {
+	u32 syscon_offset;
+};
+
+static const struct sun55i_gmac_variant sun55i_a523_gmac200 = {
+	.syscon_offset = 0x34,
+};
+
+static const struct sun55i_gmac_variant sun60iw2_gmac200 = {
+	.syscon_offset = 0x00,
+};
 
 /* RMII specific bits */
 #define SYSCON_RMII_EN		BIT(13) /* 1: enable RMII (overrides EPIT) */
@@ -40,6 +61,7 @@
 static int sun55i_gmac200_set_syscon(struct device *dev,
 				     struct plat_stmmacenet_data *plat)
 {
+	const struct sun55i_gmac_variant *variant = device_get_match_data(dev);
 	struct device_node *node = dev->of_node;
 	struct regmap *regmap;
 	u32 val, reg = 0;
@@ -95,7 +117,7 @@
 				     phy_modes(plat->phy_interface));
 	}
 
-	ret = regmap_write(regmap, SYSCON_REG, reg);
+	ret = regmap_write(regmap, variant->syscon_offset, reg);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to write to syscon\n");
 
@@ -139,7 +161,10 @@
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id sun55i_gmac200_match[] = {
-	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200" },
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200",
+	  .data = &sun55i_a523_gmac200 },
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200",
+	  .data = &sun60iw2_gmac200 },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sun55i_gmac200_match);
